course: dictionary
lesson: 7361
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A plea is a strong, heartfelt request, often for help. When a word has more than one meaning, the context tells you which one. «Giving to known charities, with a grown-up, is safer than giving to a viral plea from a stranger.» The clues are charities, grown-up, stranger and viral, so plea means a heartfelt request for something, here money.
explain: Plea has a second meaning in courts of law. A person accused of a crime makes a plea: «guilty» or «not guilty». Look for clues such as court, judge or accused. People also say «make a plea» or «enter a plea» when they speak in court.
explain: Plea can also mean an excuse or reason someone gives. «He left early on the plea that he felt ill.» This sentence tells you the reason he gave, not a request. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Plea is a noun. One is a plea, and more than one are pleas.
fact: «Plea» means a strong, emotional request, as in «a plea for help».
fact: In court, a plea is what the accused says: «guilty» or «not guilty».
fact: «Plea» can also mean an excuse or reason given, as in «on the plea that he was ill».
fact: Useful phrases: make a plea, enter a plea, a plea for help. The context shows which meaning is in use.
exercise: «Giving to known charities, with a grown-up, is safer than giving to a viral plea from a stranger.» What does plea mean here? | A small bag of food | *A strong, emotional request | A type of weather | A court case
exercise: «In court, the accused had to enter a plea.» What is a plea in this sentence? | A shop sign | A cup of tea | *What the accused says, such as guilty or not guilty | A type of song
exercise: «He left early on the plea that he felt ill.» What does plea mean here? | A loud cry for help | A form of music | A law about pets | *An excuse or reason given
test: «The lawyer asked the judge to hear the accused's plea.» What does plea mean here? | A kind of sport | *What the accused says in court | A loud noise | A dish of soup
test: «Her plea was that the bus was late, so she could not come on time.» What does plea mean here? | A loud noise | A kind of tune | *An excuse or reason given | A strong request for money
exam: «The old man's plea for peace moved everyone in the hall.» What does plea mean here? | A court verdict | *A strong, emotional request | A kind of cake | An excuse for being late
